    <h1>Shaders Guide</h1>
    <p class="sub">Real-time lighting, shadows, waving water and god rays - in ten minutes.</p>
    <div class="quick-answer"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> install Iris + Sodium (Fabric or NeoForge), download a shader pack like Complementary Reimagined or BSL, drop the .zip in the shaderpacks folder and pick it in Video Settings &rarr; Shader Packs.</div>
    <h2>Install shaders step by step</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Install your loader with <strong>Iris Shaders</strong> and <strong>Sodium</strong> - see our <a href="/mods/install-mods-java/">install guide</a>.</li>
      <li>Download a shader pack from its official page (Modrinth or CurseForge). You get a .zip file - do not unzip it.</li>
      <li>In game: Options &rarr; Video Settings &rarr; Shader Packs &rarr; Open Shader Pack Folder, and drop the .zip in.</li>
      <li>Select the pack in the list. Done.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Which shader pack</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Complementary Reimagined</strong> - the community favorite: gorgeous but tasteful, keeps the vanilla feel, great on mid-range PCs.</li>
      <li><strong>Complementary Unbound</strong> - the cinematic big sibling with more dramatic skies.</li>
      <li><strong>BSL Shaders</strong> - bright, soft and colorful; a classic that runs well almost everywhere.</li>
      <li><strong>MakeUp - Ultra Fast</strong> - for weaker PCs and laptops; huge quality per frame.</li>
      <li><strong>Photon</strong> - a modern open-source pack with impressive clouds and water.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Performance expectations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Any dedicated GPU from the last years runs Complementary/BSL at 60+ FPS with Sodium. Integrated graphics: use MakeUp or disable shadows.</li>
      <li>Shaders only change visuals - your world, mods and achievements are untouched.</li>
      <li>Pair with Distant Horizons for the full screenshot-mode experience (it needs Iris support enabled in its settings).</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>On Bedrock: Vibrant Visuals</h2>
    <p>Bedrock Edition has no shader packs like Java, but Mojang added <strong>Vibrant Visuals</strong> (an official graphics upgrade with directional lighting, shadows and volumetric fog) in the Chase the Skies drop - enable it in video settings on supported devices. Third-party "shaders" for Bedrock exist as resource packs but do far less than Java shaders.</p>
  </div>
